ROAST.PET FRONTIER STACK SCANNER 1 useful find: Tencent Hunyuan AuK /
AuK-Flash =E2=80=94 TEST NOW

Source: https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/AuK
Project: https://auk-project.github.io/
Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08936
Release: 2026-09-09; material runtime updates 2026-09-13 and 2026-09-16.

WHAT CHANGED
AuK itself is an open 1.5B speech-generation/editing foundation model, but
the fresh delta is deployability. On Sep 13 the project added official MLX
inference support for Apple Silicon plus CPU offload for CUDA. On Sep 16 it
reduced encoder memory by ~7.5 GiB, making local inference substantially
more practical. AuK-Flash is the distilled 4-step version; the authors
report ~4.5=C3=97 wall-clock speedup over the full model under matched
conditions.

ROAST.PET CAPABILITY
One local model can cover zero-shot/instruction TTS, voice cloning, content
edits, speed/pitch changes, emotion/timbre/accent edits, speech
enhancement, denoising/dereverberation and source separation. This is
unusually aligned with the Roast.pet audio factory because we can generate
a take and then alter delivery =E2=80=94 e.g. faster setup, pause before pu=
nchline,
angrier/deader-pan delivery =E2=80=94 without rebuilding the entire voice s=
tack.

INPUT / OUTPUT
Natural-language instruction + optional reference/source audio -> generated
or edited audio. Outputs are up to roughly 30 seconds in the documented
release, sufficient for Roast.pet clips.

INSTALL / API ROUTE
Python >=3D3.10 from the official GitHub package/weights on Hugging Face or
ModelScope. Official ComfyUI integration exists. AuK-Flash is the
latency-oriented checkpoint. Sep 13 added MLX Apple Silicon support and
CUDA CPU offload.

PRICING
Open weights/code: $0 model/API fee. Real cost is GPU/local compute.

COMMERCIAL LICENSE
MIT. The official LICENSE explicitly covers the released training code,
inference code, parameters and weights and permits commercial use/sale
subject to the MIT notice. Any cloned/reference voice still needs
appropriate rights/consent.

PRIVACY / SELF-HOSTING
Strong: fully self-hostable. Customer-derived scripts/reference audio can
stay on our own compute rather than being sent to a voice SaaS.

QUALITY / LATENCY CONSTRAINTS
AuK-Flash trades the full sampler for four inference steps. Author claims
need benchmarking on short comedic synthetic delivery, unusual pet-persona
voices, names/slang and exact punchline timing. The model is 1.5B but its
semantic conditioning stack means total runtime footprint is not equivalent
to a plain 1.5B TTS model; the new ~7.5 GiB encoder-memory reduction is
therefore important.

EXACT ROAST.PET USE CASE
RoastSpec -> AuK-Flash generates N deliveries -> instruction edits
promising takes (=E2=80=98more deadpan=E2=80=99, =E2=80=98faster setup=E2=
=80=99, =E2=80=98pause before final
phrase=E2=80=99, etc.) -> STT integrity gate -> ComedyRanker -> animate onl=
y
winner. Secondary use: clean customer/reference audio locally before voice
conditioning.

SMALLEST PROTOTYPE
Take 25 canonical roast lines containing names, slang and deliberate
pauses. For each: (1) generate with AuK-Flash; (2) create 3
instruction-edited deliveries; (3) score exact-word integrity, name
pronunciation, timing, emotional controllability, identity consistency,
real-time factor, VRAM and cost; (4) compare with the current hosted TTS
route. Also test whether editing an accepted take preserves exact words
better than regenerating N independent takes.

DECISION: TEST NOW. Do not replace production TTS until it wins on usable
comedic takes per dollar and exact-script reliability.
TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. AuK-Flash as local VoiceRenderer + delivery editor.
   2. Qwen3.8-Omni as semantic audiovisual ProductionQC.
   3. PixVerse V6 / H3 / Wan / HD-V1 fixed hard-pet video benchmark.
   4. Local PetPrep -> deterministic fur/edge/identity QC before paid
   inference.
   5. N-way voice -> STT integrity -> ComedyRanker -> animate winner ->
   AV-QC -> upscale accepted output only.

CHEAPEST MEANINGFUL CAPABILITY IMPROVEMENT
AuK is $0 marginal API cost on owned/already-rented compute, and the fresh
memory reduction makes that proposition materially more practical. Local
PetPrep remains effectively free as well.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR
Not a new video model: a single MIT-licensed local speech checkpoint can
now plausibly replace separate TTS, voice-editing, denoise and separation
services, while its latest update cuts encoder memory by ~7.5 GiB.

CONCRETE STACK SIMPLIFICATION
Define one VoiceService: generate(), edit_delivery(), enhance(),
separate(). Implement AuK/AuK-Flash behind it first, keep hosted providers
as fallback. Roast.pet owns RoastSpec, comedic ranking and QC rather than
provider-specific speech plumbing.

No other newly released/materially improved item found in the fresh scan
cleared the Roast.pet relevance and verification threshold; mature
unchanged tools were excluded.

